# Protected Assets — DO NOT MODIFY WITHOUT EXPLICIT USER REQUEST

## Protected HTML Elements

These elements must NEVER be changed unless the user explicitly asks to change them:

### `home-landing-topbarv2` brand lockup (in ALL prototype files)
```html
<div class="home-landing-brand-lockupv2">
  <img class="home-brand-leftv2" src="assets/napa-logo.png" alt="Carrier logo" />
  <div class="home-brand-dividerv2" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <img class="home-brand-salesforcev2" src="assets/salesforce-logo.svg" alt="Salesforce logo" />
</div>
```

### `home-flow-card-logo` logos (in `ajg-affinity-enrollment-start-here-prototype.html`)
```html
<!-- NAPA card -->
<div class="home-flow-card-logo">
  <img class="home-flow-logo-napa" src="assets/napa-seal.png" alt="NAPA" />
</div>

<!-- AFT+ cards (all three) -->
<div class="home-flow-card-logo">
  <img class="home-flow-logo-aft" src="assets/aft-logo.png" alt="AFT+" />
</div>
```

## Protected Local Asset Files

These files in `design-system-2-starter-kit/assets/` must NEVER be replaced, overwritten, or deleted without an explicit user request:

| File | Used for |
|------|----------|
| `napa-logo.png` | Top bar left logo (carrier) |
| `napa-seal.png` | NAPA home flow card logo |
| `salesforce-logo.svg` | Top bar right logo |
| `aft-logo.png` | AFT+ home flow card logos & AFT disability header/footer |
| `timer-pause-icon.svg` | Timer pause state icon (two bars) |
| `timer-play-icon.svg` | Timer resume state icon (play triangle) |
| `restart-icon.svg` | Restart flow button icon |
| `calendar-icon.png` | Date picker calendar icon |

## Rules

- NEVER replace any of the above `src` paths with Figma CDN URLs (`figma.com/api/mcp/asset/...`).
- NEVER overwrite the above asset files when fetching fresh Figma assets — always write to a new filename first.
- NEVER modify the CSS classes `home-landing-brand-lockupv2`, `home-flow-card-logo`, `home-flow-logo-napa`, `home-flow-logo-aft` without being asked.
- If a Figma fetch returns a new URL for any of the above logos, download to a temp file for review — do NOT replace the existing protected asset directly.
